# Every text file is stored and checked out as LF.
#
# On Windows this repo is checked out with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites
# text files to CRLF in the working tree. That breaks three checks that all
# assume LF, in ways that only show up on a Windows machine:
#
#   * gofmt treats CRLF as unformatted, so `gofmt -l` reports files that CI
#     (a Linux checkout) considers clean.
#   * `go run ./cmd/openapi -check` compares docs/openapi.json byte for byte
#     against a freshly generated LF document.
#   * prettier enforces endOfLine: lf in the frontend.
#
# Pinning it here makes a Windows checkout agree with CI. Every committed blob
# is already LF, so this changes no file content.
* text=auto eol=lf
